Title: Wonderwall
Artist: Oasis
Key: F# minor
Tempo: 86
Time: 4/4

# **In the key the recording sounds in, not the key it is fingered in.** Oasis
# play Em7 / G / Dsus4 / A7sus4 shapes with a capo at the second fret, so every
# published chart is a whole tone flat of the record. Transposed here: Em7→F#m7,
# G→A, Dsus4→Esus4, A7sus4→B7sus4, Cadd9→D. A chart in E minor would grade as a
# system two semitones sharp, which is the exact reading the transposition sweep
# exists to tell apart from a harmony error.
#
# Two chords to a bar and two bars to the loop, which is the recording's own
# harmonic rhythm: the intro's four passes of the riff run 0:00 → 0:22 at 86 bpm,
# so a cycle is two bars and not four.
#
# Sus and add tones are written as the triads the app's grammar can carry — the
# recording's Esus4 is emitted as E, its B7sus4 as B. Quality beyond the third
# is not graded (see grade_chart.py), so this loses nothing measurable.

